# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on
# every platform.
#
# This is not a preference. `gui/stream.py` and `bsp/load.h` had CRLF in
# their blobs while every other text file had LF, which is invisible
# from macOS and unworkable from Windows: with `core.autocrlf=true` git
# normalises the working tree to LF and compares it against a CRLF blob,
# so any real edit to those two files showed as the whole file rewritten
# - 657 deletions and 759 insertions to change ten lines - and buried
# the change it was supposed to show. Both were normalised in the same
# commit that added this file.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content and leave it alone;
# the explicit rules below are for the cases where a wrong guess would
# corrupt the file rather than merely annoy someone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.bin   binary
*.elf   binary
*.rar   binary
*.zip   binary

# Keep vendored, checksummed 3D CAD assets byte-for-byte, including the
# upstream switch model's CRLF endings.
hardware/mega-proto-carrier/models/kicad/*.step binary
hardware/reference/arduino-due/models/**/*.step binary

# Preserve the original model archive, which exceeds GitHub's normal
# per-file limit. The usable extracted STEP models remain ordinary files.
hardware/reference/arduino-due/models/source/arduino-due-1.snapshot.12.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Retain original vendor EAGLE text, including upstream whitespace.
hardware/reference/arduino-due/*/source/*.sch -whitespace
hardware/reference/arduino-due/*/source/*.brd -whitespace

# Shell scripts and the linker scripts are read by tools that do not all
# tolerate CR, and are named here so the rule survives someone relaxing
# the line above.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ld    text eol=lf
